# Keeping the build context small matters: everything not excluded here is
# uploaded to the daemon (or to Render's builder) on every single build.

# Mobile app - the API image has no use for it, and node_modules alone is
# hundreds of megabytes.
mobile/

docs/
database/
.github/
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
!backend/**/*.md

# Build output. Copying host bin/obj into the image is worse than useless: it
# can shadow the container's own restore with artifacts built against a
# different runtime and produce baffling errors.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/

# Local-only state
**/logs/
**/storage/
**/uploads/
**/receipts/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/TestResults/
**/*.user

# Secrets must never enter an image layer - a layer is readable by anyone who
# can pull it, and deleting a file in a later layer does not remove it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
